- **P6 — CLI board, wait/last, verify** (cli). No ARIA. Literal pins and assert_cmd assert the non-TTY modes, and the portable-pty outer PTY asserts the TTY-only behaviours, on `ubuntu-latest`:
  - linear static output: under the outer PTY, `waiting: <name>` appears exactly once on stderr and the stream contains no `\r` redraw, cursor-movement or erase sequence (no spinner); under non-TTY the `waiting:` line is absent;
  - `[NN/NN] … pass|fail`;
  - **cli mirror:** a literal pins the caption order the deferred 0.2.0 page must share (NAME · LIVE · STATUS · WHEEL · DIALOG · CLI), not a trycmd case: the `CAPTION` literal in the root case `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` (`tests/cli_list.rs`) and the unit case `board_row_caption_and_default_row_are_the_literals` (`src/human/board/`), chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list.
  - no SGR under non-TTY / `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` / `--json`;
  - under the outer PTY, every SGR span sits beside its word (amber only on `DIALOG`, dim only on stale rows, bold only on NAME column values), and `unable` / `fail` carry no SGR; as built (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-output-discipline) `viola list`'s spans are checked under the outer PTY by `cross_list_rows_style_each_span_beside_its_word_on_a_terminal` (bold NAME, amber only on `DIALOG`) and at the unit tier by the `board_row_style_*` cases; dim only on stale rows is proven at the unit tier (`board_row_style_a_stale_row_is_dim_end_to_end_and_only_dialog_is_amber`) and under the outer PTY (the stale-row witness, below); `viola wait` and `viola --help` carry no ESC byte and no lone CR (`tests/support/sgr.rs` `redraws`);
  - C0/C1 escaped (security excerpt, C0/C1 escaping; ratified T5 for `list` rows), checked with assert_cmd on `ubuntu-latest`:
    - Setup: human-mode `viola wait` / `viola last` run against a `viola-fake-agent` event whose text carries C0 and C1 control bytes (including ESC / CSI), and `viola list` runs against a `claude agents --json` fixture row carrying the same bytes plus `\n` / `\t`. As built (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board) `viola list` makes one `claude agents --json` read and prints every unwrapped NAME (the row's `sessionId`, never a `ViolaName`) through `escape_row` on one line, held by the `board_row_*` units and by `tests/cross_list_rows.rs` in three modes (piped, `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb`, the outer PTY; the no-ESC assertion in each mode); beside them the row escape is held by unit cases on a recorded CLI version carrying ESC, C1, DEL, `\n` and `\t`, each printed as `\xHH` (`escape_row_shows_every_control_character_as_hex_text`, `board_row_cli_cell`), and the root cases `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` and `list_of_a_stopped_wrapper_is_an_empty_board` assert no ESC and no non-ASCII byte on either stream.
    - Pass condition: each injected control appears only in escaped form. In `wait` / `last` text `\n` / `\t` stay raw. In `list` table rows `\n` / `\t` are escaped too (`\x0A`, `\x09`), so every row stays one fixed-width line.
    - Under non-TTY, `wait` / `last` stdout contains no raw C0 / C1 byte other than `\n` / `\t`, and `list` stdout contains none inside a row. Under the outer PTY, the injected controls are escaped, and viola's own SGR stays beside its word only.
  - These stand in for SC 1.3.2, 1.4.1 and 3.3.1, with no conformance claim.

- Jobs wired today in `ci.yml` (7, every one green on ci#42288148289): `test` (on `ubuntu-latest`; one harness `run --coverage` through the `sh` shim (`scripts/agent-run.sh`), i.e. the instrumented nextest run as suite `coverage` with the floors 85/95/80, followed by doctest, then the boot → status → logs → cleanup lifecycle; `AGENT_RUN_KEEP_HOMES=1`; then, in obs-plan §9 order: `jq --version`, G2 (`scripts/g2-zero-panics.sh --probe && scripts/g2-zero-panics.sh`), G4 `schema-check` (`id: schema-conformance`), the `if: failure()` harness capture, and `secret-scan` (`id: secret-scan`, `if: always()`). The uploads are gated on that scan: `diag-<os>` and `junit-<os>` on `always() && steps.secret-scan.outcome == 'success'`, `harness-<os>` (`target/agent-run/` minus `target/agent-run/chunk.diff`, the file the scan skips) on `failure() && … == 'success'`, and `secret-scan-<os>` on `always() && … == 'failure'`, all with actions/upload-artifact v7.0.1 and 7 days (`junit-<os>` carries `target/nextest/ci/junit.xml` alone); last, an `if: always()` `Gate verdict` step runs `gate --require coverage,doctest`). `perf` (on `ubuntu-latest`, `fail-fast: false`, `contents: read`, `AGENT_RUN_KEEP_HOMES=1`; test-plan §9 Perf row) runs checkout, toolchain, rust-cache, `cargo install --locked hyperfine@1.20.0`, `jq --version`, `agent-run run --perf`, then G2 (probe then check), `schema-check` and `secret-scan` (`id: secret-scan`), all `if: always()`; it uploads `perf-<os>` (`target/agent-run/artifacts/perf-*.json`) and `diag-perf-<os>` (`target/e2e-home/**/diagnostics/*.ndjson`) only on `always() && steps.secret-scan.outcome == 'success'`, and `secret-scan-perf-<os>` on a scan failure; last, an `if: always()` `Gate verdict` step runs `gate --require perf`. `test` and the pre-push carry no perf step. `ci.yml` runs no mutation job: mutation testing runs only through `agent-run run --mutants` [`--file`] (a whole member with `--package <member>`), kept for the epoch-boundary `/andromeda-code-audit` (test-plan §10 Mutation gate). `msrv` (ubuntu, rust-cache `key: msrv`) runs `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=1.96` steps for `rustc --version`, `cargo check --workspace` and `agent-run run --unit`, then `gate --require nextest-unit`. `fuzz-replay` (ubuntu, no cache) runs `agent-run run --fuzz-replay`, then `gate --require fuzz-replay`. `lint` (on `ubuntu-latest`: target job 3, then target jobs 1 and 2, the ripgrep install, `rg --pcre2-version`, G1 and G3 verbatim from obs-plan §9, `scripts/lint-probes.sh`, then `rmcp features (exactly server + transport-io, non-vacuous)` (`bash scripts/rmcp-features.sh`, after `Lint probes`; chunk 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers), then `Install cargo-modules` and `Module orphans (per lib/bin target)`: `scripts/orphans-check.sh --probe && scripts/orphans-check.sh`). `release` (on `ubuntu-latest`, `fail-fast: false`, rust-cache: target job 6) runs `scripts/release-check.sh --probe`, then `scripts/release-check.sh`; like `lint` it is a plain exit-code job, with no upload and no `viola-harness gate` step. `supply-chain` (ubuntu) runs:
  - target job 4 as `cargo deny --format json check`;
  - the `Fuzz lockfile audit (advisories, sources)` into `target/supply-chain/deny-fuzz.json`;
  - the sole-root `deny-sync.toml` tokio ban per listed sync crate, then `bash scripts/channel-tokio-free.sh` (`viola-channel`'s normal graph without its feature; both in the step `Tokio ban per sync crate (sole root)`, chunk 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers);
  - `scripts/deny-probes.sh` and `zizmor --format=json .github/workflows/`.

  Its JSON reports are uploaded from `target/supply-chain/` as artifact `supply-chain` with `if: always()`. Every gate step is fail-closed `shell: bash`.

- **P6 — CLI board, wait/last, verify** (cli). No ARIA. Literal pins over `std::process::Command` assert the non-TTY modes, and the portable-pty outer PTY asserts the TTY-only behaviours, on `ubuntu-latest`:
